dzn: Build a storage view of slices of a 3D image as a 3D view

OpenGL ES 3.1 binds one layer of a 3D texture to an image unit
(glBindImageTexture with layered GL_FALSE), which ANGLE turns into a 2D
Vulkan view of one slice of the 3D image. Dozen made a Texture2D unordered
access view of the 3D resource, an invalid call D3D12 answers by removing
the device: every Vulkan device on it is lost, and the Android VM went down
(dEQP-GLES31 image_load_store 3d *_single_layer, Intel UHD 770 and RTX 4080
Laptop GPU under WSL2).

Build it as a Texture3D unordered access view of those slices
(FirstWSlice, WSize), as Dozen already does for the render target view of
a 2D view of a 3D image.

Generated-by: LLM

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_image.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_image.c
